    "title": "Clone remote agents into the local harness",
    "intro": "Today's nightly introduces a single, focused capability: you can now take a remote swarm agent and spin up a local copy of its configuration without disturbing the original. The change spans a new server endpoint, network client support, and a dedicated UI flow in the Agent Info panel.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "9:19 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-08-09T16:19:27.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-08-09T16:19:27.000Z",
        "title": "Clone a remote agent to a local one",
        "summary": "A new end-to-end flow lets users fork a remote swarm agent's portable configuration into a fresh local agent, with an explicit contract about what gets copied and what doesn't.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Added a dedicated clone endpoint on the agents API that projects a remote swarm agent's role, personality, system prompt, skills, and icon into a new local agent, while guaranteeing the source is never mutated (source_preserved is an invariant of the handler, not a best-effort promise).",
            "commit_shas": [
              "6ad975e260b849c1b274def9d6768ca40e4925fb"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Introduced a Clone Agent to Local modal in the Agent Info panel and Sidekick taskbar, so users can name the new local agent (defaulting to a `<source>-local` name) and see the copy report before committing.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "6ad975e260b849c1b274def9d6768ca40e4925fb"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "The response returns a structured copy report listing which fields were copied vs. deliberately left behind, so users don't mistake a configuration clone for a transfer of secrets or runtime state.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "6ad975e260b849c1b274def9d6768ca40e4925fb"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Extended the Rust network client and TypeScript agents API with matching clone-to-local calls, backed by new server and UI tests covering the happy path and modal behavior.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "6ad975e260b849c1b274def9d6768ca40e4925fb"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Clone a remote agent into a local one from the Agent Info panel",
      "New server endpoint preserves the source and returns an explicit copy report",
      "Available across Desktop builds for Linux, macOS, and Windows"
